course: dictionary
lesson: 2938
title: Words that show how something is done
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. Many end in -ly, like dreamily, and they answer the question how.
explain: «The Rat is amazed, and dreamily tells him there is nothing half so much worth doing as simply messing about in boats» and then he crashes into the bank. The clues show he is not paying attention to the river, so dreamily means in a faraway, lost-in-thought way.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: "The Rat tells him, lost in his own thoughts, that there is nothing better than messing about in boats." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Dreamily is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something.
fact: «Dreamily» means in a dreamy way, as if half asleep or thinking about something far away.
fact: «Dreamily» can also mean in a soft, gentle, pleasant way.
fact: The Mole gazes dreamily at the river, which shows he is lost in thought.
fact: The forms are dreamily, more dreamily and most dreamily.
exercise: «The Rat is amazed, and dreamily tells him there is nothing half so much worth doing as simply messing about in boats.» What does dreamily show about the Rat? | *Lost in his own thoughts, not really paying attention | He is counting the boats | He is running very fast | He is shouting angrily at the Mole
exercise: «The Mole gazes dreamily at the river.» What does dreamily mean here? | Quickly, as if in a race | Very loudly | *As if far away, lost in thought
exercise: «The Mole gazes dreamily at the river.» Find and copy the word that tells how the Mole looks. | gazes | river | *dreamily | Mole
test: «She hummed dreamily as she rocked the baby to sleep.» What does dreamily mean here? | *Softly and gently, in a peaceful, pleasant way | Loudly and angrily | Quickly, to finish the job
test: Anya says dreamily means very fast. What is the right meaning? | Very cold | Very fast, like a race car | *Slow and far away, or soft and gentle | Very angry and loud
exam: Which word means nearly the same as dreamily when someone is lost in thought? | *Absent-mindedly | Quickly | Angrily | Loudly
